module examples.err_layout_runtime_nests_dma

# plans/M10.md item A2, 03-hardware.md §3.1: nesting is the `runtime` kind's
# own allowance, and it is exclusive in both directions — only a `runtime`
# layout may nest another, and only a `runtime` layout may be nested. §3.1
# gives the reason directly: a `runtime` layout "is not device-visible — no
# device reads or writes it, so it is neither a `dma` payload nor an `mmio`
# register map".
#
# This pins the direction a real mistake takes: a runtime table reaching for
# a device structure it happens to have declared nearby. The opposite
# direction (a `dma` layout nesting a `runtime` one) is the same rejection
# from the same function and is covered in
# `sema::types`' own `declaration_shape_guards` table, next to the M7 item E
# gap it must not be confused with — a `dma` layout nesting another `dma`
# layout is a missing feature (`err-layout-nested`), while crossing the
# `runtime` boundary is a permanent rule.

@layout(dma, endian=little)
struct BlkReqHeader:
    kind: u32
    reserved: u32


@layout(runtime, endian=little)
struct TurnTable:
    rr_cursor: u64
    pending: BlkReqHeader
